  "notes": "{乗|の}り{越|こ}える is a transitive verb ({他動詞|たどうし}) meaning to overcome or to ride past.\n\nETYMOLOGY:\n- {乗|の}る (to ride) + {越|こ}える (to cross over) → to ride over/past\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{乗|の}り{越|こ}えている indicates a state of having overcome or being in the process.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {困難|こんなん}を{乗|の}り{越|こ}える (overcome difficulties)\n- {危機|きき}を{乗|の}り{越|こ}える (get through a crisis)\n- {壁|かべ}を{乗|の}り{越|こ}える (overcome a barrier)\n- {駅|えき}を{乗|の}り{越|こ}える (ride past a station)\n\nUSAGE:\nMost commonly used figuratively to describe overcoming challenges, difficulties, or emotional hardships. The literal meaning of riding past a stop is also common.",
